WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.060
Imagine running a country,
with four dials on your desk.

2
00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:06.600
You want fast growth, plenty of jobs,

3
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:08.810
steady prices, and no big,

4
00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:11.090
lasting deficit with the world.

5
00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:13.120
And the planet matters.

6
00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:18.950
UK emissions fell by about 50
per cent from 1990 to 2022,

7
00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:20.000
as the economy grew.

8
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.930
So can a country grow fast,

9
00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:25.010
keep everyone in work
and hold prices steady,

10
00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:26.610
all at the same time?

11
00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:29.780
In this mission, you'll find
out how these goals are linked,

12
00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:32.410
and what happens when you push one hard.

13
00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:35.920
Then you'll test what different
policies do to each dial,

14
00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:39.430
and why choosing between
goals is about values.

15
00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:42.990
Your mission: find out whether
a country can have it all,

16
00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:44.670
and what it costs to try.
